#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8b9014e-32cf-5f04-856c-7fd663bea50f" :question/math-academy-id "e-528" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8e6c58c-da62-5dab-8325-a53c14d9b8ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-529" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x.\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+Cx+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$ We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab40a4d3-c418-5b64-a04c-bb017155a4d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-530" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $y'  = 2x,$ and sketch the solution curves of this equation." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29a0265e-ad88-5ac9-88fe-878aa4f0d0bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-531" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$$\nf'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0) = 2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C \\\\ 2 & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)+C \\\\ 2 & =0+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe1ffa70-41ba-592d-9221-889fddb97a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289748} {:answer/id #uuid "5e89e576-486a-554f-a8e4-561e6e58ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289749} {:answer/id #uuid "abe66a86-26ba-52ce-ae99-cda0b40a5423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289750} {:answer/id #uuid "d68943c3-babc-5cca-bb4a-6060331890a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289751} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d5de22-29dc-571a-9a04-6e24438dc027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e89e576-486a-554f-a8e4-561e6e58ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289749} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4971da-77d9-5b10-9742-4958f510bb24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae4d3203-76af-57e6-914e-e9a022b4a7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-119032" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "578e6903-379c-5efb-aac9-852cc8534b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{(3x-1)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289755} {:answer/id #uuid "f582ebf3-cef1-57ae-8af2-3001deecf27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{3}{(x-1)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289756} {:answer/id #uuid "40debac3-e06b-513d-a96c-22874472f6e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289757} {:answer/id #uuid "7fcf3473-3770-5267-8bff-e44925e2c035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289758} {:answer/id #uuid "48ca5459-c7c2-5216-8d87-70f58dd6dcf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fcf3473-3770-5267-8bff-e44925e2c035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289758} :answer-field/id #uuid "45707a41-bc4b-5405-b387-28496c1d2308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "026bb192-a837-5fcc-8667-53e2260d5753" :question/math-academy-id "q-119034" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{x-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{3}{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5df53c4f-461b-58da-b708-fe15732e2635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289762} {:answer/id #uuid "8adbc7d2-6f0c-5a4b-8810-f0c4038f4edd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289763} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab4224b-f455-5ab1-8988-6720dea5f79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289764} {:answer/id #uuid "5d634642-3a2b-5db5-8bf9-7acfea5de072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(3-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289765} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf1bfe2-3b08-5429-a12d-2fdcda9de7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf1bfe2-3b08-5429-a12d-2fdcda9de7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289766} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b665f02-3442-53c7-bbf5-d87277631ced" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36c02825-1f2e-5058-9fc1-074753d8120c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+6{x}^{2}=4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4x-6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27334472-5810-5336-9487-b0301e071ae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2(x+9{e}^{-3x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289769} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb27748-2e8a-51fe-b114-fd69e9fbf3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x-2{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289770} {:answer/id #uuid "480c3fa0-3814-569b-865a-4f09ecea8bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x+{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289771} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4f2e08-81d5-5c75-a13a-ea6f71eb90ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x-18{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289772} {:answer/id #uuid "af6db5b9-065f-579a-8c62-b840cd841d3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2(x-3{e}^{-3x})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eb27748-2e8a-51fe-b114-fd69e9fbf3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=x-2{e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289770} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b52d1da-f2b1-59c0-bf0b-cbabcae3fd2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e422fe9-fc97-5df0-b6a5-ce1fd6f9f5cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119037" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)-6{e}^{-3x}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =1+6{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+6{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+6\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+6(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x}) \\\\  & =x-2{e}^{-3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc74e732-0426-58ed-8b06-8d2337394f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289776} {:answer/id #uuid "341ae6c4-1c86-5ec2-b2af-0ede991b9440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289777} {:answer/id #uuid "572afa50-c153-5c64-a089-521ae475a9cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289778} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b9e3f6-fb70-5efc-8893-be9f6e3062bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289779} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f9b4b4-38ac-5987-89d5-ae02e4fb3121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1b9e3f6-fb70-5efc-8893-be9f6e3062bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289779} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d519aa3-8736-5012-8052-19588bd5ca8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3f71093-8817-517a-8348-8c70d7a0bd9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-119041" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-8(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f76c7bc8-5f0f-5691-b0f5-d5e342b0537e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289783} {:answer/id #uuid "38ff9b99-6f09-5946-b632-57cf62d75cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289784} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a27261-a5ca-518c-8c7b-d480e13742a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289785} {:answer/id #uuid "76c484bc-cbc4-5551-a1f8-91f030aab2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289786} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc024df-0d20-5b15-bcc3-a94f7517d89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c484bc-cbc4-5551-a1f8-91f030aab2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289786} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d4af72-1848-578c-907a-e3c3e65ecc24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75c31897-52bd-540c-a546-ce6303ed7371" :question/math-academy-id "q-119043" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d14e0df1-3bb8-5197-b25c-bc87e8eef3d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289790} {:answer/id #uuid "4f766d19-73fe-5c00-851c-def3a95b1697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289791} {:answer/id #uuid "b25c8c97-b577-5dfa-9d6d-9b976fd446bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289792} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb0664d-836b-5d5d-aeb4-68ec1251deba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289793} {:answer/id #uuid "73d0e6bb-117a-5547-ad15-e6a24ca686e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f766d19-73fe-5c00-851c-def3a95b1697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289791} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9fb5778-ba1b-563c-934c-4d2eafdbb97b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a18f6dbb-80c9-5e0a-b091-fdf4e8634a66" :question/math-academy-id "q-119045" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+C \\\\ -1 & =-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc26178d-66e1-5cb6-bb45-849d2d988af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+3x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289797} {:answer/id #uuid "f06eafbb-f26e-5dee-8e2e-3259ad93187f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}+2x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289798} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c1a9f8-df13-59fa-b6f7-c083b9c7a619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289799} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd2de54-1f98-5c77-af73-45b76afbcf8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289800} {:answer/id #uuid "0ab54013-ab23-5f19-99d7-88e171fd9ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ab54013-ab23-5f19-99d7-88e171fd9ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289801} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b32a5a9-2cdb-5a34-962d-d790d2f978b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b51e635-ecb6-5289-b3c9-ec6e11e4a7b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119046" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)-4x=1$ that satisfies the condition $f(1)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4x+1.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(1)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =2(1)^{2}+1+C \\\\ -1 & =2+1+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc1d25b9-f7e3-57a0-a200-c248abd2cb33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289804} {:answer/id #uuid "b6811527-a888-5f7d-9068-c826b2d11450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x+{e}^{x/2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289805} {:answer/id #uuid "1f553902-9e9a-5efe-b0e1-8d16f790d45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289806} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b0ce7b-fb84-5ecf-8423-8c307d36227a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289807} {:answer/id #uuid "e415321f-c23f-526c-833a-532d2d8ad940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f553902-9e9a-5efe-b0e1-8d16f790d45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289806} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bee9e7d-b007-5273-96a3-5b6ec18e2c42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "038b8c53-512a-5090-8c56-bdb0d2e76789" :question/math-academy-id "q-119083" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2x={e}^{x/2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+{e}^{x/2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{e}^{x/2})\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & ={0}^{2}+2{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 2 & =0+2(1)+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f13730-32d0-5fe7-a4c3-f7572848e72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/557708220ba3876b0ae9dbf1d265d11e8d98cf1102ad084d93419543ede35c4b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289811} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f19b5e-0cb6-5f83-a9a0-36d844b5b2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/