n{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/cc2ee25a85be3ffdb055853f7665bd53d34003a74b96a14bb947bed39b18e83f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f81d7a23-b6bb-555f-8b6e-e6951a88794c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/d5f4f2b65878b9c152b5c87e1fac0473f0e76455fc5762ba10f21555d68a60c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289818} {:answer/id #uuid "8261b1ff-bc73-55dd-b5a7-c1022af26cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/a65cbd746c3bb9abe495af168fd7c63e83ecf3d942c5fb478f3d7d312d140b4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289819} {:answer/id #uuid "53b0e08e-406e-5506-8b7d-bc2a778b94db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289820} {:answer/id #uuid "5d99d12f-c09f-538f-a9f4-426942ead7ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/95b3d8fc43562341f93a2bccbcbe36d2a070a2dd6687606175ab5e9580f86e2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289821} {:answer/id #uuid "e69ac199-3b5b-5b77-9585-00467bfaa84a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/0d14e369d621a6c2d06b4db1485ff43f6af4be2014e9d26564c9ca11e9bd38cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b0e08e-406e-5506-8b7d-bc2a778b94db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289820} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fb09f07-f81d-53d1-91f3-0c78a9b393f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a05048db-be50-5d0c-8e66-1eb6eda34260" :question/math-academy-id "q-119142" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\int (x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e0ff2e64925dcd8bdf298c47815f6e2982fe6091e1ff5dea042f585c67ef1721.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a772853-58d2-56db-991e-ec65fe8d0aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{x+1}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a772853-58d2-56db-991e-ec65fe8d0aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{x+1}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289825} :answer-field/id #uuid "27fbb802-818f-528e-a38b-34520e907660" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c774207f-e833-51f4-b6a4-47a8e4f76e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-352068" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x+1}\\,{y}^{′}=4$ that satisfies the condition $y(3)=10.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int (x+1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(2(x+1)^{1/2})+C \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(3)=10$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =8\\sqrt{3+1}+C \\\\ 10 & =8(2)+C \\\\ C & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=8\\sqrt{x+1}-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27bafd7e-a0cd-5785-88a0-c17e11e4a36d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/5c933988eb335b7310387cfc532a6e144de3e43bfebde4c29d1e5fe76fa35027.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289828} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c1a271-dbb8-57ad-a54c-cc63075b3c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/763db9d469cdd9047ec823966fc922726c97cb22e6cd848a432f26bc5e6529d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289829} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c78633-e85c-52b5-8346-8d471fc66157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/8910d0342d03d546117091ccd19378905b8cfc3644997cfe3ca7d95a3b4e7a6f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289830} {:answer/id #uuid "7db96fae-3b22-5ee5-a9d3-b86b06ae924a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/4a2aefaff6332175608a37f6532bafd5be4ccb60a2aad8e4400a0f5767c4588a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289831} {:answer/id #uuid "36962595-cfc5-5593-8096-3776d0d8346d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/aae99f368b61351b9163646b70ea0b085019d6935334422ccb398958a81d1e47.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27bafd7e-a0cd-5785-88a0-c17e11e4a36d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/5c933988eb335b7310387cfc532a6e144de3e43bfebde4c29d1e5fe76fa35027.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289828} :answer-field/id #uuid "a849ded1-39d0-5cbf-be3d-fcd6bb0075cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0290b966-ea8a-5aaa-95c5-d4ed0c24c604" :question/math-academy-id "q-49947" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x>0?$" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C,\\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/8e047c3c27a000af943f50499f8c7559acceeb78cc006e796c7d353729991517.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991a4d75-b082-5ddb-9e0e-daec82c04821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095672} {:answer/id #uuid "b018b6ae-1940-5995-bcd3-0cb355cdfdbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-4e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095673} {:answer/id #uuid "c2357d5d-526c-504c-b3d2-09cc85042828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095674} {:answer/id #uuid "eed6b0a7-f89a-5f99-8fa6-663cdc54a4e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095675} {:answer/id #uuid "5a53ae9e-07c4-5848-85e2-a1c6b214ea93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991a4d75-b082-5ddb-9e0e-daec82c04821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095672} :answer-field/id #uuid "144fd343-32aa-51c0-ba1c-2d78f454b0d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb82aa2f-3e4a-523a-94c2-c95aa3cb8ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-50136" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89aee0c2-41c4-50d9-95e7-d07999f8e43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095678} {:answer/id #uuid "a8264bab-88eb-5c1b-8cf6-4b5658e50c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Cx^{2} + 10x + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095679} {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095680} {:answer/id #uuid "0a099fae-b25d-5abb-a50a-c5dc1eda7e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095681} {:answer/id #uuid "1a40f9c2-33a9-5233-bec8-c51acd272979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095680} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c860608-75a8-5451-a1a7-a0683cdbc84f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17751a3b-ed4b-5966-a450-330460c02715" :question/math-academy-id "q-50139" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-10.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-10\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-10x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-10\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D \\\\  & =-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113c25f7-34d8-597a-9d18-6e2a6ffa7ace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289835} {:answer/id #uuid "32d3c70f-8bd8-5ce8-b6f6-f8e361f906a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289836} {:answer/id #uuid "a0491e6f-f72a-552c-a54d-7b7411e89373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289837} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8ba3ba-6fed-5713-a29b-e5a693af1a4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289838} {:answer/id #uuid "73a3e9fd-1914-52e9-a145-05bd26f2d97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0491e6f-f72a-552c-a54d-7b7411e89373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289837} :answer-field/id #uuid "53fdc3f8-2079-5b4a-b8fc-969e00cb264d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6ab78bb-c8ea-5de6-abd1-a27ba2080dba" :question/math-academy-id "q-50146" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-4(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-2(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87248665-cb5c-5039-a61b-f40377bba96f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095696} {:answer/id #uuid "ca53b3f7-7fae-554a-ae0b-ae63a12f5e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095697} {:answer/id #uuid "e65a9044-67d3-586d-be0f-d72ddf67972d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095698} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdad7c2-d1f6-5540-909f-d9988ae726bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095699} {:answer/id #uuid "5e919e55-cc7c-5065-9aea-29667e6de4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cdad7c2-d1f6-5540-909f-d9988ae726bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50196-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095699} :answer-field/id #uuid "71784ece-a52d-5f27-a140-7ccee85a3e0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27b042e7-c453-5f49-bac9-de5985bbacde" :question/math-academy-id "q-50196" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3(x+1)^{2}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3\\int (x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3\\int (x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(x+1)^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/03a5bf5134dc7d551b2602145c4c25081a2ad274f02c95845e5789b288e618a1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd855587-99f3-505e-97c3-1301d8ab4a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/18a0a935932bbe409ceb7e36459a2091ee46b74829c873bfc048a71f543d8eff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289842} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7db587-abe5-59ed-bd47-170916b1d8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/90beec07c4d15fa823aee98c8a1a1e6c58846bb9b713b84848e010cc98cb3ca3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289843} {:answer/id #uuid "8f2d28d6-668f-51ed-bc6c-0fd102ab483a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/1cf05351f0353e95dbdff8f620f6e920650d505be88edb3e61486676cb59357c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289844} {:answer/id #uuid "e90149a1-91a5-5118-84e1-7822ad71dc7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/7d23f940448475b1da1008ab1d3270236abec662208e81bd0de9355e85103a38.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289845} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3cb31b-69a0-5b6a-baf6-0887bb0a3a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/3670e1b40ce25af5974059a86c502cfb68f80e81746cbb162805ab7ae4a6bce2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b7db587-abe5-59ed-bd47-170916b1d8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/90beec07c4d15fa823aee98c8a1a1e6c58846bb9b713b84848e010cc98cb3ca3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289843} :answer-field/id #uuid "97a3a653-59a6-54f3-b434-8384602bd8e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4a52539-fba9-529d-8223-251824b4bbce" :question/math-academy-id "q-50197" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1=0$ for $x>0?$" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1$ for $x>0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/c837c3b617fa49f3d081d961196a954fada99b8d7cd12b7d7f729232e16be066.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c3fce9-4dba-553f-ac4e-8bfd541b9ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}\\,{x}^{3/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289849} {:answer/id #uuid "aedeec53-0f33-5a00-8f0d-b977e85a66c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289850} {:answer/id #uuid "d53425a6-b517-5529-84f7-bdeb700529b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289851} {:answer/id #uuid "7377d739-2959-5629-a400-637f3e350a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{5}\\,{x}^{3/2}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289852} {:answer/id #uuid "50d7837b-7f89-5a83-a114-cabd6f5e3bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d53425a6-b517-5529-84f7-bdeb700529b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289851} :answer-field/id #uuid "120b1a92-69b2-5d1e-8d09-cb723185099c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "354406fe-0ae4-5318-84e4-271686e8ea87" :question/math-academy-id "q-79554" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\sqrt{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}\\,{x}^{5/2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d8f248-ae63-510e-b122-9cc55b03b498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289856} {:answer/id #uuid "3c5d5149-c7c9-5986-b904-15c30d057288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289857} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8ca706-8cc9-584d-af55-bd7b1a5d58e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289858} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b1d254-8ff3-512c-baa4-107f102cdb2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289859} {:answer/id #uuid "c839da2e-4863-51c2-8d8f-686bcf43ef5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c839da2e-4863-51c2-8d8f-686bcf43ef5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289860} :answer-field/id #uuid "c776fff4-3270-5ba6-96b2-d459273f208a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dcbbed7-1234-55a1-9c74-3ded079b3151" :question/math-academy-id "q-8311" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4=0$ given that $y(-1)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-4x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=4$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =-4\\cdot (-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =4+C \\\\ 0 & =C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-4x\\,.\n$$"}]}
